---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Aperture from "../components/Aperture.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
const notes = (await getCollection("notes")).sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
const featured = notes[0];
---
<Base title="Waking Matter" description="Memory, provenance and evaluation infrastructure for AI agents. Explore Waking Matter’s public code and research questions." canonical="https://wakingmatter.com/" tone="void" current="home">
  <main id="content">
    <div class="hero-band">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="label hero-eyebrow">Building systems for cumulative intelligence</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Agents should improve with experience.</h1>
          <p class="hero-deck">We build memory, provenance and evaluation infrastructure for agents working with changing information.</p>
          <a class="hero-cta" href="#work">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-figure"><Aperture class="hero-aperture" /></div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section id="memory" class="band" aria-labelledby="memory-title">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <p class="label">The problem</p>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="memory-title">Memory is not enough.</h2>
          <p>A stored answer can be outdated. A successful procedure can fail when the task changes. Keeping more history does not tell an agent what to trust or do next.</p>
          <p>The challenge is to connect retained experience to decisions, and to notice when the past has become a liability.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="work" class="band" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <p class="label">Public technical work</p>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="work-title">Agent Memory Contracts</h2>
          <p>An agent’s interpretation should not silently become a fact. Agent Memory Contracts is a public Python library for making that boundary explicit.</p>
          <p>Source evidence stays linked to a candidate claim. Accepting the claim requires a recorded decision, and the validator rejects a trusted record without the required authorization. The worked reducer example shows acceptance, rejection and an invalid promotion.</p>
          <div class="work-links">
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/avs-io/agent-memory-contracts">Inspect the code and tests <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/avs-io/agent-memory-contracts/blob/main/examples/reference_reducer.py">Run the worked example <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="questions-label">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="band-head"><p class="label" id="questions-label">What we are investigating</p><p class="label">01 / 04</p></div>
        <div class="trait-grid question-grid">
          <article class="trait"><span class="meta num">01</span><h2>Decisions</h2><p>When should a previous outcome change the next search, test or action?</p></article>
          <article class="trait"><span class="meta num">02</span><h2>Useful state</h2><p>Which facts, procedures and failed attempts deserve to persist, and with what source and scope?</p></article>
          <article class="trait"><span class="meta num">03</span><h2>Revision</h2><p>How should a system detect stale knowledge and decide what to revise or reset?</p></article>
          <article class="trait"><span class="meta num">04</span><h2>Evaluation</h2><p>Does retained experience improve results when context, compute and prior advice are accounted for?</p></article>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/research/">Explore the research questions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <p class="label">Repeated work</p>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="workflows-title">Bring a problem that keeps coming back.</h2>
          <p>Does an agent reconstruct the same context every week, repeat a known mistake or fail when a fact changes? We want to work on recurring workflows where the result can be checked and a person can intervene.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@wakingmatter.com">Tell us about your workflow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    {featured && <section class="band" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <p class="label">The broader thesis</p>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="thesis-title">Intelligence should accumulate.</h2>
          <p>Learning costs time, attention and failed attempts. The essay asks what should survive that investment, how it can pass between systems and when it should lose authority.</p>
          <p class="meta">{featured.data.pubDate.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}{featured.data.updatedDate && <> · Updated {featured.data.updatedDate.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</>}</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`/notes/${featured.slug}/`}>Read the essay <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>}
  </main>
</Base>
